{title: Be True to Your School}
{artist: The Beach Boys}
{key: G}
{tempo: 144}
{duration: 2:00}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
When [G]some loud braggart tries to [Em]put me down
And says his [Am]school is great
[D7]I tell him right away
Now [G]what's the matter, buddy, ain't you [Em]heard of my school
It's number [Am]one in the state
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C/D]So be true to your [G]school
Just like you would with your [B7]girl or guy
Be true to your [Em]school now
And let your colors [Eb7]fly[A7]
Be true to your [Am]school_[D]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I got a [G]letterman's sweater with a [Em]letter in front
I got for [Am]football and track
[D7]I'm proud to wear it now
When [G]I cruise around the other [Em]parts of the town
I got a [Am]decal in back
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C/D]So be true to your [G]school
Just like you would with your [B7]girl or guy
Be true to your [Em]school now
And let your colors [Eb7]fly[A7]
Be true to your [Am]school_[D]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
On [G]Friday we'll be jacked up on the [Em]football game
And I'll be [Am]ready to fight
[D7]We're gonna smash 'em now
My [G]girl will be working on her [Em]pom-poms now
And she'll be [Am]yelling tonight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C/D]So be true to your [G]school
Just like you would with your [B7]girl or guy
Be true to your [Em]school now
And let your colors [Eb7]fly[A7]
Be true to your [Am]school_[D]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_part: Outro}
[G]Rah rah rah, be [Em]true to your school
[Am]Rah rah rah, be [D]true to your school
